<header><p class="st-kicker">chiefdom · Central and Southern Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Bondelswarts</h1><p class="st-meta">1800 CE – 1906 CE (approx.) · capital Warmbad</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Nama community of southern Namibia centred on Warmbad, known for its uprisings against German and later South African rule.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Bondelswarts, in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nama-people">Nama</a> !Gami-ǂnun, were a Khoekhoe-speaking Nama group living north of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orange-river">Orange River</a>. In 1805 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london-missionary-society">London Missionary Society</a> founded a mission at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/warmbad">Warmbad</a> among them, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/methodism">Wesleyans</a> took it over in the 1830s; Warmbad became the seat of their kapteins.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Like other <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nama-people">Nama</a> communities they were governed by a hereditary kaptein, here of the Christian family, with a council of elders. They lived by herding <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cattle">cattle</a>, sheep and goats in the dry south, traded with the Cape and many adopted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christianity">Christianity</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cape-dutch">Cape Dutch</a> through the mission.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1903 the killing of their kaptein <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jan-abraham-christian">Jan Abraham Christian</a> by German officials sparked a rising, which merged into the wider <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nama-people">Nama</a> war; they made peace at Ukamas in December 1906 and lost most of their land. Their 1922 rebellion against a South African dog tax was crushed with aircraft.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="chiefdom, 1800 CE – 1906 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><ellipse cx="44" cy="56" rx="16" ry="24"/><path d="M44 34 V78"/><path d="M68 20 V84"/><path d="M68 20 L63 30 H73 Z"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">chiefdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Central and Southern Africa</p><div class="st